# 03 - select(), withColumn(), drop() (PySpark Practical)

This practical covers:
- select()
- selectExpr()
- withColumn()
- drop()
- alias()
- rename columns
- multiple column operations

---

## 0) Setup

```python
from pyspark.sql import SparkSession
from pyspark.sql.functions import col, lit

spark = SparkSession.builder     .appName("SelectWithColumnDrop")     .master("local[*]")     .getOrCreate()

data = [
    (1, "Pramod", "IT", 50000),
    (2, "Akash", "HR", 60000),
    (3, "Rahul", "IT", 45000),
    (4, "Neha", "Finance", 70000)
]

df = spark.createDataFrame(data, ["id", "name", "dept", "salary"])
df.show()
```

---

## 1) select() (Most Common)

```python
df.select("id", "name").show()
```

---

## 2) select() using col()

```python
df.select(col("id"), col("dept"), col("salary")).show()
```

---

## 3) alias() (Rename in select)

```python
df.select(
    col("id"),
    col("name").alias("employee_name"),
    col("salary").alias("monthly_salary")
).show()
```

---

## 4) selectExpr() (SQL Style)

```python
df.selectExpr(
    "id",
    "name",
    "salary",
    "salary * 12 as annual_salary"
).show()
```

---

## 5) withColumn() (Add/Modify Column)

### 5.1 Add new column

```python
df2 = df.withColumn("country", lit("India"))
df2.show()
```

---

### 5.2 Modify existing column

```python
df3 = df.withColumn("salary", col("salary") + 5000)
df3.show()
```

---

## 6) drop() (Remove Column)

```python
df4 = df.drop("dept")
df4.show()
```

---

## 7) Rename Columns (2 ways)

### 7.1 withColumnRenamed()

```python
df5 = df.withColumnRenamed("dept", "department")
df5.show()
```

---

### 7.2 Rename multiple columns (recommended)
Use toDF():

```python
df6 = df.toDF("emp_id", "emp_name", "department", "salary")
df6.show()
```

---

## 8) Summary

- select() is used to pick columns.
- alias() renames columns during selection.
- withColumn() is used to add/modify columns.
- drop() removes unwanted columns.
- withColumnRenamed() renames one column.
- toDF() renames all columns at once.

